{"diagnosis": "Fetch makes no progress with max_addr=0x00000000 and TRAP: no progress, so no instruction fetch ever completes. In mem_state 0 line 584 sets mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word instead of its inverse, deasserting mem_valid on normal fetches and stalling the bus. This contradicts the line 598 assert mem_valid == !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word, confirming inverted polarity from a missing `!`.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -582,7 +582,7 @@
 				0: begin
 					if (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata) begin
-						mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
+						mem_valid <= !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
 						mem_instr <= mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst;
 						mem_wstrb <= 0;
 						mem_state <= 1;
 					end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: no progress, max_addr advances beyond 0x00000000 with fetch progress"}

